&P252006 = CUSAS 10, 11 
#atf: lang akk 
@tablet 
@obverse 
1. [pi2-ta-ar]-ra#-as-si pi2-ta-ar-ra-as!-<si> 
#tr.ts: pitarassi pitarassi 
#tr.en: Keep her apart! Keep her apart! 
2. [ma-ra]-at# a-ni-im ni-pi2-ih sza-me-e 
#tr.ts: mārāt anim nipiḫ šamê 
#tr.en: The daughters of Anum, (in) the rising of the sky, 
3. [u4?-ma?]-am u2-ul-li-la-a-ma 
#tr.ts: ūmam ullilamma 
#tr.en: purified the day(?), 
4. [sza]-me-e sza _an-na_ 
#tr.ts: šamê ša anim 
#tr.en: and the heaven of Anum. 
5. i-ba-asz-szi ra-mu-um e-li ni-szi i#-ha#-ap#-pu#-up 
#tr.ts: ibašši râmum eli nišī iḫappup 
#tr.en: Love was happening, upon the people it was caressing(?). 
6. ra-mu-um li-ih-pu-pa-am i-na s,e#-ri#-ia# 
#tr.ts: râmum liḫpupam ina ṣēriya 
#tr.en: May love caress(?) me! 
7. lu-ud-di lu-uq-bi lu-ta-wu-u2 lu#-ra#-'i3#-im 
#tr.ts: luddi luqubi lutawû lura’īm 
#tr.en: Let me cast (a spell), let me command, let me speak, let me love. 
8. hu-us-si2-ni-ma ki-ma asz-nu-ga#-[a]-li# 
#tr.ts: ḫussinnima kīma ašnugalli 
#tr.en: Think of me as an ašnugallum-snake 
9. li-ih-szu#-szu# pa-nu-ki! ki-ma ri-im-ti-[im] 
#tr.ts: liḫšušū pānūki kīma rīmtim 
#tr.en: Let your face rejoice like a wild cow. 
10. e tu-usz-bi a-na mi-li-ik a-bi-ki# 
#tr.ts: ē tušbī ana milik abiki 
#tr.en: May you not wait for your father's consent. 
11. e te-el-qe-e mi-li-ik um-mi-[ki] 
#tr.ts: ē telqe milik ummiki 
#tr.en: May you not take your mother’s advice. 
12. szum-ma qa2-asz-da-at# im-da-sza li#-x 
#tr.ts: šumma qašdat imdaša li-... 
#tr.en: If she is a q.-woman, may she ... her obligation to work. 
13. szum-ma na-di-a-at# bi-bi-il-sza li#-x 
#tr.ts: šumma nadīat bibilša li-... 
#tr.en: If she is an n.-woman, may she ... a marriage gift. 
14. szum-ma ke#-ez-re-et li-ka3-ap-pi2-ir asz#-ta-ma-sza e-li-ia li-im-qu2-ut# 
#tr.ts: šumma kezret likappir aštammaša eliya limqut 
#tr.en: If she is a prostitute, may she clean her tavern and upon me fall. 
15. szi-[ip]-tum# u2-ul ia-tu 
#tr.ts: šiptum ul yâttu 
#tr.en: The incantation is not mine, 
16. szi-pa#-at# e2-a u3 {d}inanna isz-ku-nu 
#tr.ts: šipat ea u ištar iškunū 
#tr.en: it is an incantation that of Ea and Ištar established.
